  "source": "A2 post-bounce values versus A8 formal reversal notation",
  "counterexample": "In E=R, V(x)=x^2/2, alpha=beta=eta=1, r=y=0, choose a prescribed event with incoming state (x,p)=(1,1). Reflection sends it to (1,-1). At the reversed event, correct reversed post-value is R(1,1)=(1,-1); naive R of original post-value is R(1,-1)=(1,1), unequal. Such incoming state is obtained by taking initial state Phi_-tau(1,1) with an interior tau and T>tau.",
  "classification": "False literal all-time equality route; source endpoint/change-of-variables interpretation remains sound.",
  "accepted_convention": "At interior reversed events exchange original pre/post states; elsewhere use R Gamma(T-s). Strictly interior event times make endpoints0,T unambiguous.",
  "scope_effect": "97 target is endpoint/time involution only. Do not add full path equality to97 to bypass later density98 work. The eventual density integral is insensitive to finite point changes, but rate factors use the incoming left-limit and must be matched exactly."
